course: dictionary
lesson: 3652
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the dictionary lists each one as a number. You choose the meaning that fits the sentence. Firm is a good example: it can describe ground, a grip, or a decision.
explain: Look at the words around firm. «A pile driver drives long posts deep into the ground to hold up buildings by carrying their weight down to firm ground.» The buildings need something solid to stand on, so firm ground must mean solid ground, not soft mud.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense. Solid ground fits. Soft ground would not keep a building up, so soft is not the meaning here.
fact: Firm means solid and not soft, and hard to press in or move.
fact: Firm can also mean strong and steady, as in a firm grip.
fact: Firm can mean not likely to change, as in a firm decision.
fact: A firm is a company or business, such as a firm that employs workers and sells goods.
fact: Firm can also mean strict but fair, as in a firm teacher.
exercise: «...carrying their weight down to firm ground.» What does firm ground mean? | Ground covered in snow | *Solid ground, not soft mud | Ground with lots of trees | Ground that is very steep
exercise: Lily keeps a firm grip on the handrail on the steep ladder. What does firm grip mean? | Wet and slippery | Painted bright blue | Loose and wobbly | *Strong and steady
exercise: Mum works for a firm that sells shoes. Find and copy the word that names a business. | shoes | sells | works | *firm
test: «Ben made a firm decision to save his money.» What does firm mean here? | Sleepy and slow | *Not likely to change | Loud and rude | Hard like a rock
test: Which word is the best swap for firm in «firm ground»? | *solid | early | sleepy | fizzy
exam: Mia says firm means floppy, like a wet sock. Why is she wrong? | Firm means floppy, but only when it is wet | Firm means quick and speedy | Firm means sweet and tasty | *Firm means solid and not soft, the opposite of floppy
